{"id": "742d6319-48c6-42ba-8bda-c8b465b13e68", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review your SageMaker async inference setup. That means the endpoint and its config, the async output and failure settings, the autoscaling policy, and the recent queue metrics.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_9iBMLyXgaWdPvJMd7JCszh", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-async-posture-review", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review the configuration posture of the SageMaker ASYNCHRONOUS inference endpoint(s) serving an LLM and identify misconfigurations that could cause silently dropped requests or a backed-up queue. This is a read-only config review, not a root-cause hunt. Use only non-mutating AWS calls.",
  "context": "User reports the async LLM endpoint 'seems to drop requests silently and sometimes the queue backs up'. They want a list of what is misconfigured. Start by finding all endpoints in the account/region whose endpoint config has AsyncInferenceConfig (list_endpoints / list_endpoint_configs / describe_endpoint_config). If more than one candidate exists, review each and say which looks like the LLM one (by name, model, instance type).",
  "resources": ["AWS account 123456789012", "region us-east-1", "SageMaker endpoints/endpoint-configs with AsyncInferenceConfig"],
  "timeframe": "Metrics/logs for the last 24h to 7d ending 2026-11-17T19:00:00Z",
  "criteria": "Check and report on: (1) AsyncInferenceConfig: OutputConfig S3OutputPath, S3FailurePath (missing failure path = silent failures), KmsKeyId, NotificationConfig (SuccessTopic/ErrorTopic/IncludeInferenceResponseIn) - are SNS topics set, exist, and have valid policies/subscriptions; ClientConfig.MaxConcurrentInvocationsPerInstance (too high/low for an LLM, default 4). (2) Variant config: instance type/count, InitialInstanceCount vs min capacity, ContainerStartupHealthCheckTimeoutInSeconds, ModelDataDownloadTimeoutInSeconds, InvocationTimeout / container timeouts (async max 1 hour; LLM long generations), model container env (e.g. SAGEMAKER_MODEL_SERVER_TIMEOUT, TS_/DJL/TGI settings, max batch/concurrency). (3) Application Auto Scaling: scalable target min/max capacity (min 0 and scale-from-zero cold starts, step scaling on HasBacklogWithoutCapacity), target-tracking on ApproximateBacklogSizePerInstance - target value, cooldowns, whether policies exist at all, max capacity cap. (4) IAM execution role access to the input/output S3 buckets, KMS, SNS (read only: just evaluate whether it looks sufficient; do not change). (5) S3 bucket config: output/failure bucket existence, lifecycle rules that may expire results early. (6) CloudWatch metrics: ApproximateBacklogSize, ApproximateBacklogSizePerInstance, ApproximateAgeOfOldestRequest, HasBacklogWithoutCapacity, InvocationsProcessed, InvocationFailures, InvocationModelErrors, RequestDownloadFailures, ResponseUploadFailures, NotificationFailures, TimeInBacklog, plus CPU/GPU/memory utilization; note spikes and when. (7) Any CloudWatch alarms on these metrics (absence of alarms on failures/backlog age is a finding). (8) Endpoint logs in /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints/<name> for timeouts, OOM, 5xx, 'Invocation timed out', model errors if easily found. Deliver a prioritized list of concrete misconfigurations/risks with the evidence (values observed) and the suggested fix for each, plus what you could not verify. Keep the report concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review SageMaker async endpoint config, autoscaling, and queue metrics"}], "created_at": null}
